1
00:00:01,106 --> 00:00:04,026
[microphone feedback]

2
00:00:04,109 --> 00:00:06,111
[♪ opening theme music playing]

3
00:00:40,646 --> 00:00:44,066
FLEX X COP 2

4
00:00:44,149 --> 00:00:46,985
CHARACTERS, PLACES, ORGANIZATIONS,
AND EVENTS IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

5
00:00:47,069 --> 00:00:49,112
ALL CHILD ACTORS AND ANIMALS
FILMED IN A SAFE ENVIRONMENT

6
00:00:52,157 --> 00:00:54,117
[♪ tense, foreboding music playing]

7
00:01:03,460 --> 00:01:05,212
[♪ music increases in tempo]

8
00:01:19,851 --> 00:01:21,311
[♪ music swells]

9
00:01:24,356 --> 00:01:25,399
Bang!

10
00:01:25,482 --> 00:01:26,483
[scoffs]

11
00:01:26,566 --> 00:01:27,609
[♪ music fades]

12
00:01:27,693 --> 00:01:28,735
Whoa.

13
00:01:28,819 --> 00:01:30,112
You didn't even blink.

14
00:01:30,195 --> 00:01:31,405
Huh? [gun clicks]

15
00:01:31,488 --> 00:01:32,614
I saw you flinch.

16
00:01:36,159 --> 00:01:38,203
I'm Jin Isoo, the owner of this place.

17
00:01:38,995 --> 00:01:40,747
And I'm a violent crime detective.

18
00:01:40,831 --> 00:01:42,749
[♪ tense pulsating music playing]

19
00:01:46,002 --> 00:01:48,088
-Is this real?
-It's real.

20
00:01:51,341 --> 00:01:52,509
A rich cop.

21
00:01:52,592 --> 00:01:53,927
[Seongwook scoffs softly]

22
00:01:54,010 --> 00:01:55,387
I really liked this place.

23
00:01:56,096 --> 00:01:57,472
Now I won't be coming back.

24
00:01:57,931 --> 00:01:59,891
Since you're here,
how about a game with me?

25
00:02:01,643 --> 00:02:05,063
If you win, I'll give you
a lifetime membership for free.

26
00:02:05,147 --> 00:02:06,565
But if I win,

27
00:02:06,648 --> 00:02:08,984
you just need to answer my questions.

28
00:02:13,321 --> 00:02:16,158
-Ever heard the word "whippersnapper"?
-No.

29
00:02:16,241 --> 00:02:18,118
I've never heard such a dated word before.

30
00:02:18,201 --> 00:02:21,246
[scoffs] That's what you are.
Look it up when you get home.

31
00:02:21,955 --> 00:02:24,499
Hey, I guess you don't feel confident.

32
00:02:26,793 --> 00:02:28,879
I heard you were
all washed up and retired.

33
00:02:28,962 --> 00:02:30,505
How dare you, you asshole.

34
00:02:30,589 --> 00:02:33,467
I'm talking with your boss here.

35
00:02:33,550 --> 00:02:34,760
Stay out of this, lackey.

36
00:02:34,843 --> 00:02:35,886
[♪ music swells]

37
00:02:37,429 --> 00:02:38,597
Not feeling confident?

38
00:02:39,431 --> 00:02:41,391
About winning against a whippersnapper?

39
00:02:43,143 --> 00:02:44,352
[♪ music fades]

40
00:02:44,436 --> 00:02:45,562
[Seongwook sighs]

41
00:02:46,730 --> 00:02:48,064
The club's management rights.

42
00:02:49,107 --> 00:02:51,401
If you want to bet with me,
make it worth my while.

43
00:02:51,485 --> 00:02:54,112
Whoa, you sure drive a hard bargain.

44
00:02:54,196 --> 00:02:55,197
Deal!

45
00:02:55,280 --> 00:02:57,449
[♪ jaunty, dramatic music playing]

46
00:02:57,532 --> 00:02:58,992
I'll shoot first.

47
00:03:06,792 --> 00:03:07,834
Pull.

48
00:03:08,251 --> 00:03:09,586
[gunshot]

49
00:03:09,669 --> 00:03:10,670
Pull.

50
00:03:11,296 --> 00:03:12,547
-[gunshot]
-[target shatters]

51
00:03:15,217 --> 00:03:16,259
[casings clatter]

52
00:03:21,598 --> 00:03:22,974
Pull.

53
00:03:23,058 --> 00:03:24,142
[gunshot]

54
00:03:24,726 --> 00:03:26,144
Pull.

55
00:03:26,228 --> 00:03:27,270
[gunshot]

56
00:03:27,646 --> 00:03:29,439
So your eyes are still holding up.

57
00:03:29,523 --> 00:03:30,565
What?

58
00:03:30,649 --> 00:03:31,650
[gun clicks]
STYLE
::cue()

59
00:03:33,944 --> 00:03:34,945
[Isoo] Pull.

60
00:03:35,487 --> 00:03:36,655
[gunshot]

61
00:03:36,738 --> 00:03:38,114
Pull.

62
00:03:44,412 --> 00:03:45,413
[Seongwook] Pull.

63
00:03:48,750 --> 00:03:49,834
Pull.

64
00:03:50,544 --> 00:03:51,586
[gunshot]

65
00:03:52,837 --> 00:03:54,130
[Isoo] Pull.

66
00:03:55,757 --> 00:03:56,925
Pull.

67
00:03:57,801 --> 00:03:58,843
[gunshot]

68
00:03:59,803 --> 00:04:00,804
[casing clatters]

69
00:04:02,305 --> 00:04:03,723
[Seongwook] Pull.

70
00:04:03,807 --> 00:04:04,808
[gunshot]

71
00:04:05,267 --> 00:04:06,476
Pull.

72
00:04:06,560 --> 00:04:07,727
[target whizzing]

73
00:04:12,774 --> 00:04:13,858
[exhales sharply]

74
00:04:14,484 --> 00:04:16,152
Looks like I won. Huh?

75
00:04:17,654 --> 00:04:19,406
Age catches up with everyone.

76
00:04:21,866 --> 00:04:22,868
[♪ music fades]

77
00:04:32,752 --> 00:04:33,753
EPISODE 8

78
00:04:33,837 --> 00:04:35,797
-[Isoo] Detective Joo.
-What happened?

79
00:04:35,881 --> 00:04:38,133
-What's with the outfit?
-Never mind that.

80
00:04:38,216 --> 00:04:40,260
Ham Seongwook says
he'll tell us everything.

81
00:04:40,343 --> 00:04:41,344
What? How?

82
00:04:41,428 --> 00:04:42,846
-[♪ jaunty music playing]
-[exhales smugly]

83
00:04:42,929 --> 00:04:44,890
I made a bet with him over this club.

84
00:04:44,973 --> 00:04:47,851
People like him can't resist a challenge.

85
00:04:47,934 --> 00:04:49,144
You know it, too.

86
00:04:49,227 --> 00:04:51,354
You made a bet with him over this club?

87
00:04:51,438 --> 00:04:53,273
-Is this yours?
-I bought it yesterday.

88
00:04:53,857 --> 00:04:56,568
The owner was deep in debt,
so he wanted to sell it quickly.

89
00:04:56,651 --> 00:04:58,945
[exhales incredulously] How much was it?

90
00:04:59,029 --> 00:05:01,197
Actually, never mind.
Why would I need to know?

91
00:05:01,281 --> 00:05:04,451
[sighs] I almost missed one shot,
so that really had me sweating.

92
00:05:04,534 --> 00:05:05,827
Because you'd lose the club?

93
00:05:05,911 --> 00:05:07,829
No, because I would lose to him.

94
00:05:07,913 --> 00:05:10,832
How could I live with myself
after losing to a washed-up thug?

95
00:05:10,916 --> 00:05:13,585
That's true.
You can't lose to a washed-up thug.

96
00:05:13,668 --> 00:05:16,421
Anyway, I got him to the table.
I did pretty well, right?

97
00:05:16,504 --> 00:05:19,799
[chuckles] Yes, you did well.
You really are a cheat code.

98
00:05:19,883 --> 00:05:22,052
[clicks tongue, sighs contentedly]

99
00:05:22,135 --> 00:05:23,261
[♪ music fades]

100
00:05:26,306 --> 00:05:28,224
I'm Joo Hyera from Gangha Police.

101
00:05:29,893 --> 00:05:30,894
[Isoo] She's my team leader.

102
00:05:30,977 --> 00:05:32,729
She'll be joining us. Have a seat.

103
00:05:34,606 --> 00:05:35,774
[exhales deeply]

104
00:05:38,985 --> 00:05:41,321
I lost, so I will keep my word.

105
00:05:41,404 --> 00:05:44,074
Oh, like a real man.

106
00:05:44,157 --> 00:05:45,325
Don't lie to us now.

107
00:05:45,408 --> 00:05:47,327
I never lie.

108
00:05:48,161 --> 00:05:51,665
On April 12th, Magician Park Jaeha
died during a performance.

109
00:05:52,457 --> 00:05:54,292
We believe he was murdered.

110
00:05:55,460 --> 00:05:58,797
Please tell us everything that happened
between you and Mr. Park Jaeha.

111
00:06:02,342 --> 00:06:03,718
[♪ soft, suspenseful music playing]

112
00:06:04,636 --> 00:06:07,681
There's an expression
about being the apple of one's eye.

113
00:06:09,349 --> 00:06:10,892
Only someone who's had a child

114
00:06:11,601 --> 00:06:13,311
can understand what that feels like.

115
00:06:15,355 --> 00:06:16,648
My daughter

116
00:06:17,524 --> 00:06:18,733
is the apple of my eye.

117
00:06:20,527 --> 00:06:22,278
When she was little,

118
00:06:22,362 --> 00:06:24,948
my wife died from an illness.

119
00:06:26,783 --> 00:06:27,951
I cherished her,

120
00:06:28,618 --> 00:06:29,911
treasured her,

121
00:06:30,912 --> 00:06:32,747
and raised her with the utmost care.

122
00:06:36,167 --> 00:06:37,752
But not long ago,

123
00:06:37,836 --> 00:06:39,879
she said she got a boyfriend.

124
00:06:40,922 --> 00:06:42,424
So I put my boys on him

125
00:06:43,758 --> 00:06:45,510
to find out what kind of guy he was.

126
00:06:47,220 --> 00:06:49,055
[♪ music turns ominous]

127
00:06:52,726 --> 00:06:53,727
But it turns out...
STYLE
::cue()

128
00:07:08,533 --> 00:07:09,659
Seven women?

129
00:07:09,743 --> 00:07:11,661
[inhales sharply, exhales]

130
00:07:11,745 --> 00:07:12,746
Yes.

131
00:07:12,829 --> 00:07:13,955
[scoffs]

132
00:07:14,038 --> 00:07:17,584
And my Sujeong is...
[in English] "Honey 7"?

133
00:07:17,667 --> 00:07:18,918
[♪ music swells]

134
00:07:26,259 --> 00:07:27,385
[♪ music fades]

135
00:07:27,469 --> 00:07:28,887
[in Korean] Bring that bastard to me.

136
00:07:29,763 --> 00:07:31,014
PARK JAEHA'S MAGIC FIRE

137
00:07:31,097 --> 00:07:32,515
[whistling]

138
00:07:33,266 --> 00:07:36,311
[in English] "Park Jaeha's Magic Fire."

139
00:07:36,394 --> 00:07:37,520
-[chuckles smugly]
-[henchman whistles]

140
00:07:37,604 --> 00:07:38,646
[whistles]

141
00:07:38,730 --> 00:07:40,315
[♪ gripping, foreboding music playing]

142
00:07:41,983 --> 00:07:43,234
Park Jaeha?

143
00:07:43,318 --> 00:07:44,569
Yes?

144
00:07:44,652 --> 00:07:45,945
Come with us.

145
00:07:46,029 --> 00:07:47,113
Who are you?

146
00:07:47,197 --> 00:07:48,364
Wait, what is this about?

147
00:07:48,740 --> 00:07:50,325
[exclaims, groans]

148
00:07:50,408 --> 00:07:52,535
-Hey, magician.
-Yes?

149
00:07:52,619 --> 00:07:54,829
Do you want us to beat you up
and drag you away,

150
00:07:54,913 --> 00:07:56,080
or will you come quietly?

151
00:07:56,164 --> 00:07:57,499
[breath trembling]

152
00:07:57,582 --> 00:07:59,000
-I'll come quietly.
-Let's go.

153
00:07:59,417 --> 00:08:00,585
[exclaims in pain]

154
00:08:02,879 --> 00:08:04,672
[♪ music swells, stops]

155
00:08:04,756 --> 00:08:06,132
Seriously, what's this about?

156
00:08:06,216 --> 00:08:10,428
Just try saying one more word.

157
00:08:10,512 --> 00:08:12,305
You'll definitely regret it.

158
00:08:12,388 --> 00:08:14,557
I think you've misunderstood something--
[exclaims]

159
00:08:14,641 --> 00:08:16,392
[♪ tense, foreboding music playing]

160
00:08:18,645 --> 00:08:19,646
Drive.

161
00:08:20,230 --> 00:08:22,023
[tires screeching]

162
00:08:22,106 --> 00:08:23,316
[♪ music swells]

163
00:08:24,943 --> 00:08:25,944
[gasps]

164
00:08:26,027 --> 00:08:27,028
[♪ music fades]

165
00:08:27,695 --> 00:08:29,322
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

166
00:08:30,949 --> 00:08:31,950
[gasps]

167
00:08:33,201 --> 00:08:34,911
I'm Sujeong's father.

168
00:08:40,750 --> 00:08:42,085
I'm sorry.

169
00:08:42,168 --> 00:08:43,795
Please forgive me just once.

170
00:08:43,878 --> 00:08:44,879
Forgive you for what?

171
00:08:47,090 --> 00:08:50,260
I'll break up with her right away,
and I won't ever see her again!

172
00:08:51,261 --> 00:08:52,303
Which means

173
00:08:53,388 --> 00:08:55,974
you never really loved her to begin with?

174
00:08:57,183 --> 00:08:58,184
What?

175
00:08:58,268 --> 00:09:00,895
You never cared about her,
but you dragged my daughter

176
00:09:00,979 --> 00:09:02,313
in and out of hotels?

177
00:09:03,773 --> 00:09:04,816
[exclaims]

178
00:09:05,650 --> 00:09:08,444
I didn't do anything to her.
We only slept holding hands!

179
00:09:09,946 --> 00:09:11,406
It's true!

180
00:09:11,489 --> 00:09:13,199
I swear on my dead mother!

181
00:09:13,908 --> 00:09:15,869
I promise! It's true!

182
00:09:17,954 --> 00:09:19,789
[♪ music increases in tempo]

183
00:09:23,293 --> 00:09:24,419
Which hand?

184
00:09:25,170 --> 00:09:26,462
We promise with the right.

185
00:09:29,799 --> 00:09:30,800
[yelps]

186
00:09:31,384 --> 00:09:32,844
Wait!

187
00:09:32,927 --> 00:09:35,096
What are you doing to me?

188
00:09:35,180 --> 00:09:36,848
I used to be in the mob.

189
00:09:36,931 --> 00:09:38,057
What?

190
00:09:38,141 --> 00:09:40,476
Our mob always pays people back in kind.

191
00:09:41,352 --> 00:09:43,521
Your hand touched my daughter,

192
00:09:43,605 --> 00:09:44,939
so I'm going to take it.

193
00:09:45,690 --> 00:09:47,442
No, you can't!

194
00:09:47,525 --> 00:09:48,943
Don't do this to me!

195
00:09:49,027 --> 00:09:50,028
Just beat me...

196
00:09:50,111 --> 00:09:51,404
[grunts, groans]

197
00:09:52,113 --> 00:09:53,823
Damn it, you hit me again.

198
00:09:53,907 --> 00:09:56,743
Wait, hold on! Please, sir, wait!

199
00:09:56,826 --> 00:09:57,911
Wait.

200
00:09:59,913 --> 00:10:00,914
If I...

201
00:10:01,831 --> 00:10:03,625
lose this hand,

202
00:10:04,584 --> 00:10:05,919
Sujeong will be sad.

203
00:10:06,002 --> 00:10:07,086
-Cut it off.
-[Jaeha] No!

204
00:10:07,170 --> 00:10:08,922
Wait, hold on!

205
00:10:09,005 --> 00:10:11,883
Please wait, sir. Please.

206
00:10:11,966 --> 00:10:13,134
Wait.

207
00:10:13,218 --> 00:10:14,636
[breathing heavily]

208
00:10:15,428 --> 00:10:16,930
Please just let me...

209
00:10:18,056 --> 00:10:19,432
do my last show. [sobbing]

210
00:10:21,476 --> 00:10:23,269
This will be the end

211
00:10:24,395 --> 00:10:26,731
of my life as a magician.

212
00:10:29,108 --> 00:10:30,610
[continues sobbing]

213
00:10:33,863 --> 00:10:36,074
No, sir, please.
STYLE
::cue()

214
00:10:36,157 --> 00:10:38,117
-[♪ music fades]
-That's all.

215
00:10:38,201 --> 00:10:40,119
My boys were just waiting there

216
00:10:40,203 --> 00:10:42,163
to bring him to me after the show.

217
00:10:43,831 --> 00:10:45,458
Would his fingers have been enough?

218
00:10:45,541 --> 00:10:48,044
She's your cherished, treasured daughter.

219
00:10:48,127 --> 00:10:49,379
[clicks tongue, inhales deeply]

220
00:10:49,462 --> 00:10:50,463
[exhales] Hey...

221
00:10:50,546 --> 00:10:52,882
I wasn't serious
about cutting his hand off.

222
00:10:52,966 --> 00:10:54,842
I was just... [scoffs softly]

223
00:10:54,926 --> 00:10:57,053
...threatening him
so he'd end things for good.

224
00:10:58,304 --> 00:11:00,932
That bastard was truly
nothing but a spineless coward.

225
00:11:03,017 --> 00:11:04,102
I'm done talking now.

226
00:11:05,687 --> 00:11:06,688
I'll be on my way.

227
00:11:06,771 --> 00:11:08,022
[Sujeong] Dad.

228
00:11:12,068 --> 00:11:13,695
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

229
00:11:14,487 --> 00:11:15,488
Oh, goodness.

230
00:11:15,571 --> 00:11:17,991
My princess. This must've been heavy.

231
00:11:18,074 --> 00:11:20,243
You said you were arriving late.
Hey, take this.

232
00:11:25,248 --> 00:11:26,249
What's wrong?

233
00:11:27,959 --> 00:11:29,043
Was it you?

234
00:11:29,752 --> 00:11:30,753
What do you mean?

235
00:11:31,462 --> 00:11:32,672
[breath trembles]

236
00:11:36,175 --> 00:11:37,218
Hey.

237
00:11:38,553 --> 00:11:39,595
[whispering] It's not loaded.

238
00:11:41,097 --> 00:11:42,098
[sighs softly in relief]

239
00:11:42,181 --> 00:11:43,850
Did you kill him?

240
00:11:44,934 --> 00:11:45,935
I didn't.

241
00:11:46,561 --> 00:11:48,479
[voice shaking] I told you I loved him.

242
00:11:49,647 --> 00:11:51,107
Were you the one who killed him?

243
00:11:58,114 --> 00:11:59,699
[breath trembling]

244
00:12:02,201 --> 00:12:04,454
If you really think I killed him,

245
00:12:05,163 --> 00:12:06,164
pull the trigger.

246
00:12:19,010 --> 00:12:20,345
[♪ music swells]

247
00:12:28,353 --> 00:12:29,437
[♪ music fades]

248
00:12:34,442 --> 00:12:35,860
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

249
00:12:39,030 --> 00:12:42,450
I'll tell you everything
about the kind of man Park Jaeha was.

250
00:12:52,710 --> 00:12:53,961
[♪ music fades]

251
00:12:54,045 --> 00:12:55,463
Can we believe him?

252
00:12:56,172 --> 00:12:57,757
He said he never lies.

253
00:13:00,760 --> 00:13:03,679
Why would he mention
that he threatened to cut off his fingers?

254
00:13:04,263 --> 00:13:06,307
He's confident because he didn't kill him.

255
00:13:06,391 --> 00:13:09,018
Or the victim's dead,
so it doesn't matter if he tells us.

256
00:13:09,811 --> 00:13:13,606
Besides, you have to mix in
a bit of truth when telling a lie.

257
00:13:13,689 --> 00:13:16,651
So you think Ham Seongwook is the culprit?

258
00:13:17,902 --> 00:13:19,112
[sighs thoughtfully]

259
00:13:19,821 --> 00:13:20,822
No.

260
00:13:21,781 --> 00:13:24,117
Ham Seongwook would've killed him quietly.

261
00:13:24,200 --> 00:13:25,952
He'd never do it onstage.

262
00:13:26,035 --> 00:13:27,036
That's true.

263
00:13:27,120 --> 00:13:28,287
[♪ soft, suspenseful music playing]

264
00:13:28,371 --> 00:13:32,250
[inhales sharply] The culprit killed him
while countless people were watching.

265
00:13:33,459 --> 00:13:34,794
That's the crux of this case.

266
00:13:37,046 --> 00:13:38,089
[♪ music fades]
STYLE
::cue()

267
00:13:43,594 --> 00:13:44,804
Excuse me.

268
00:13:44,887 --> 00:13:46,931
Oh. Yes, can I help you?

269
00:13:47,849 --> 00:13:49,308
I'm with the police.

270
00:13:49,392 --> 00:13:50,893
Oh, right.

271
00:13:54,021 --> 00:13:57,441
This is you in this photo, isn't it?

272
00:13:58,192 --> 00:13:59,944
Uh, yes, it's me.

273
00:14:00,653 --> 00:14:03,322
Did you notice anything strange
on the day of the incident?

274
00:14:03,406 --> 00:14:05,241
[scoffs softly] Anything strange?

275
00:14:05,324 --> 00:14:07,034
Yes, anything out of the ordinary.

276
00:14:07,952 --> 00:14:09,120
Uh...

277
00:14:10,163 --> 00:14:13,166
[sharp inhale]
That day, I was quite worn out.

278
00:14:14,041 --> 00:14:15,084
I don't know why.

279
00:14:15,168 --> 00:14:18,504
I thought maybe it was because
I had a drink the night before,

280
00:14:18,588 --> 00:14:21,257
but the equipment felt heavy.

281
00:14:21,340 --> 00:14:22,341
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

282
00:14:22,425 --> 00:14:23,926
-Heavy?
-Yes.

283
00:14:26,596 --> 00:14:29,640
Did you see Mr. Park Jaehyung
at the workshop that day?

284
00:14:30,975 --> 00:14:32,560
No, I didn't.

285
00:14:32,643 --> 00:14:34,687
He usually comes out
to check the equipment,

286
00:14:34,770 --> 00:14:36,647
but he wasn't there that day.

287
00:14:37,857 --> 00:14:39,567
-Okay, thank you.
-Sure.

288
00:14:53,873 --> 00:14:56,042
[♪ suspenseful, foreboding music playing]

289
00:15:11,933 --> 00:15:13,059
[sighs softly]

290
00:15:18,022 --> 00:15:19,440
[♪ music increases in tempo]

291
00:15:32,912 --> 00:15:34,288
[♪ music resumes tempo]

292
00:15:35,915 --> 00:15:39,669
ORAL MEDICATION
PARK JAEHYUNG

293
00:15:39,752 --> 00:15:41,629
[♪ suspenseful, ticking music playing]

294
00:15:41,712 --> 00:15:42,797
[pen clicks]

295
00:15:47,093 --> 00:15:48,135
[pen clicks]

296
00:15:48,219 --> 00:15:49,553
[♪ music swells]

297
00:15:50,888 --> 00:15:51,973
[♪ music fades]

298
00:15:52,056 --> 00:15:53,057
[sniffs]

299
00:15:53,432 --> 00:15:54,433
[sniffs]

300
00:15:57,812 --> 00:15:59,605
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

301
00:16:07,697 --> 00:16:09,198
-[jerry can thuds]
-[kerosene sloshing]

302
00:16:21,043 --> 00:16:22,295
-Hello.
-Hello.

303
00:16:23,587 --> 00:16:25,923
I'm Detective Choi Kyungjin
from Gangha Police.

304
00:16:26,007 --> 00:16:27,341
Ah, right.

305
00:16:27,425 --> 00:16:29,885
Did anyone buy kerosene
from here recently?

306
00:16:29,969 --> 00:16:31,887
I think there were a few.

307
00:16:31,971 --> 00:16:33,597
Could you check for me?

308
00:16:33,681 --> 00:16:34,974
Of course.

309
00:16:36,350 --> 00:16:37,518
[exhales softly]

310
00:16:38,686 --> 00:16:40,521
[♪ music increases in tempo]

311
00:16:45,276 --> 00:16:46,694
[♪ music swells]

312
00:16:48,612 --> 00:16:50,364
-[chuckles softly]
-[♪ music fades]
STYLE
::cue()

313
00:16:53,034 --> 00:16:54,327
[Isoo] Mmm...

314
00:16:54,910 --> 00:16:57,788
If Ham Seongwook isn't the killer...

315
00:16:57,872 --> 00:16:59,874
Let's think this through
from the beginning. [sighs]

316
00:17:01,334 --> 00:17:05,421
The three women
who have access to the equipment.

317
00:17:05,504 --> 00:17:06,756
And also,

318
00:17:06,839 --> 00:17:08,466
Park Jaehyung.

319
00:17:10,968 --> 00:17:12,386
[Isoo sighs thoughtfully]

320
00:17:12,470 --> 00:17:13,596
[Hyera sighs softly]

321
00:17:16,807 --> 00:17:17,850
Where were you?

322
00:17:17,933 --> 00:17:19,060
[sighs wearily]

323
00:17:19,643 --> 00:17:21,354
I went to the theater.

324
00:17:21,437 --> 00:17:23,522
Park Jaehyung wasn't
in the workshop that day.

325
00:17:23,606 --> 00:17:24,607
Huh?

326
00:17:25,441 --> 00:17:26,484
Then what happened?

327
00:17:27,443 --> 00:17:28,778
He was there when we went.

328
00:17:28,861 --> 00:17:30,571
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

329
00:17:33,824 --> 00:17:35,368
Mr. Park Jaeha?

330
00:17:38,204 --> 00:17:39,497
I'm Park Jaehyung.

331
00:17:40,289 --> 00:17:41,415
Jaeha's brother.

332
00:17:41,499 --> 00:17:42,917
The staff didn't see him.

333
00:17:43,000 --> 00:17:46,087
And there was a heater in the workshop.

334
00:17:46,170 --> 00:17:47,213
A kerosene heater.

335
00:17:47,296 --> 00:17:48,756
The kerosene can was half empty.

336
00:17:53,094 --> 00:17:55,304
I found out who bought the kerosene.

337
00:17:57,890 --> 00:18:00,101
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

338
00:18:00,184 --> 00:18:03,062
No one bought kerosene
from gas stations near the theater,

339
00:18:03,729 --> 00:18:05,815
so I checked the suspects' neighborhoods.

340
00:18:05,898 --> 00:18:06,982
[keyboard key clacks]

341
00:18:31,924 --> 00:18:33,050
[keyboard key clacks]

342
00:18:33,843 --> 00:18:35,010
That's Ms. Lee Jiyun.

343
00:18:35,094 --> 00:18:37,388
I told you! I was right.

344
00:18:38,264 --> 00:18:41,809
Lee Jiyun and Park Jaehyung
were working together.

345
00:18:41,892 --> 00:18:45,062
[sighs smugly]
God, my instincts are unbelievable.

346
00:18:45,146 --> 00:18:46,397
He might be right.

347
00:18:47,648 --> 00:18:51,485
I found medication in his workshop.
I checked with the hospital.

348
00:18:51,569 --> 00:18:53,070
He has terminal cancer.

349
00:18:53,154 --> 00:18:54,196
No way.

350
00:18:54,739 --> 00:18:55,781
[sighs softly]

351
00:18:59,535 --> 00:19:01,579
On the verge of death,

352
00:19:01,662 --> 00:19:04,081
he wanted to kill his brother,
whom he was jealous of?

353
00:19:04,665 --> 00:19:06,083
[sighs deeply]

354
00:19:06,167 --> 00:19:08,169
He must've felt so wronged, huh?

355
00:19:08,252 --> 00:19:11,172
He's going to die anyway,
so why not take his brother with him?

356
00:19:11,255 --> 00:19:14,049
And Ms. Lee Jiyun joined his plan
after being betrayed.

357
00:19:20,681 --> 00:19:23,559
[Hyera] Park Jaehyung poured kerosene
into the equipment.

358
00:19:28,898 --> 00:19:29,982
[in English] Okay.

359
00:19:31,567 --> 00:19:33,986
[Hyera, in Korean] And Lee Jiyun
pretended not to know?

360
00:19:34,695 --> 00:19:36,030
Find out where Lee Jiyun is.

361
00:19:36,113 --> 00:19:37,198
Got it.

362
00:19:45,247 --> 00:19:46,290
[♪ music fades]

363
00:19:46,373 --> 00:19:47,500
DIRECTOR LEE JIYUN

364
00:20:02,348 --> 00:20:03,390
-[sighs]
-[box snaps shut]

365
00:20:05,142 --> 00:20:06,143
[knock at door]

366
00:20:10,898 --> 00:20:12,775
-[Hyera] Ms. Lee Jiyun.
-Yes?

367
00:20:12,858 --> 00:20:15,194
-[door closes]
-[Hyera] Can we have a word with you?

368
00:20:15,277 --> 00:20:16,946
-Sure.
-[Isoo] Oh...

369
00:20:17,530 --> 00:20:19,698
-It looks like you were packing.
-[Jiyun, softly] Mmm.

370
00:20:20,491 --> 00:20:22,243
The show's over now.

371
00:20:23,285 --> 00:20:24,662
I need to find another project.

372
00:20:24,745 --> 00:20:25,746
[Isoo] Mmm...

373
00:20:26,705 --> 00:20:27,957
So, what can I do for you?

374
00:20:28,791 --> 00:20:31,377
Two days before the incident,
at Sankyeong Gas Station,

375
00:20:31,460 --> 00:20:32,920
you bought kerosene, didn't you?

376
00:20:34,964 --> 00:20:35,965
Yes, I did.

377
00:20:36,048 --> 00:20:37,049
Why?

378
00:20:37,842 --> 00:20:39,677
-To kill the one who betrayed you?
-What?

379
00:20:40,261 --> 00:20:41,262
[Isoo inhales sharply]

380
00:20:41,345 --> 00:20:44,557
You gave your boyfriend of one year
money to get a place together,

381
00:20:44,640 --> 00:20:47,601
only to find he had seven girlfriends.
You must've been furious.

382
00:20:47,685 --> 00:20:49,311
I understand. Mmm.

383
00:20:50,020 --> 00:20:52,064
What are you talking about?

384
00:20:53,148 --> 00:20:55,484
We found kerosene inside the casket.
STYLE
::cue()

385
00:20:55,568 --> 00:20:56,610
[♪ tense music playing]

386
00:20:56,694 --> 00:20:59,446
You're the only one
who bought kerosene before the incident.

387
00:20:59,530 --> 00:21:01,740
Jaehyung asked me to buy it for him.

388
00:21:02,741 --> 00:21:04,785
The workshop gets cold,
so he uses a heater.

389
00:21:05,744 --> 00:21:07,663
He can't go out in a wheelchair to buy it.

390
00:21:07,746 --> 00:21:09,039
Mmm...

391
00:21:09,123 --> 00:21:12,167
Is that all you did for him?
I have a feeling you did more.

392
00:21:12,918 --> 00:21:16,338
Why are you doing this to me?
I'm already pissed off as it is.

393
00:21:16,422 --> 00:21:19,258
You knew he was going to kill
his brother, didn't you?

394
00:21:20,301 --> 00:21:21,927
You knew and looked the other way.

395
00:21:22,011 --> 00:21:23,012
Or...

396
00:21:23,804 --> 00:21:25,347
were you in on it from the start?

397
00:21:25,973 --> 00:21:27,433
[Jiyun] Detective.

398
00:21:28,058 --> 00:21:30,227
I'm not that dumb.

399
00:21:31,562 --> 00:21:32,813
Of course, I'm angry.

400
00:21:32,897 --> 00:21:34,690
It wasn't just another woman or two.

401
00:21:35,316 --> 00:21:37,359
But I didn't know that
until after he died.

402
00:21:38,152 --> 00:21:39,987
Even if I had known,

403
00:21:40,863 --> 00:21:43,324
why would I ruin my life
over a bastard like that?

404
00:21:44,283 --> 00:21:45,576
I'd get caught this quickly.

405
00:21:45,659 --> 00:21:47,620
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

406
00:21:50,247 --> 00:21:53,959
If you're still that suspicious,
I'll do a polygraph, or whatever it takes.

407
00:21:55,961 --> 00:21:57,254
I'll do it all!

408
00:21:59,048 --> 00:22:00,090
[♪ music swells]

409
00:22:02,885 --> 00:22:03,928
[♪ music fades]

410
00:22:04,011 --> 00:22:06,555
NATIONAL FORENSIC SERVICE

411
00:22:09,141 --> 00:22:10,935
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

412
00:22:12,645 --> 00:22:13,896
[camera shutter clicking]

413
00:22:20,486 --> 00:22:22,154
[Dr. Yoon] I'll begin the autopsy.

414
00:22:33,248 --> 00:22:34,708
[♪ music increases in tempo]

415
00:22:53,018 --> 00:22:54,019
[grunts softly]

416
00:22:57,773 --> 00:22:59,024
[♪ music resumes tempo]

417
00:22:59,817 --> 00:23:02,528
The older one had cancer,
the other was hunted by thugs.

418
00:23:04,363 --> 00:23:05,364
Uh...

419
00:23:06,407 --> 00:23:07,700
But why didn't he run away?

420
00:23:08,450 --> 00:23:09,785
[Hyera] What?

421
00:23:09,868 --> 00:23:12,413
Ham Seongwook was going to cut off
his fingers that day.

422
00:23:12,496 --> 00:23:14,248
Why didn't he run away?

423
00:23:19,920 --> 00:23:20,921
[sniffs]

424
00:23:21,505 --> 00:23:23,340
[gasps softly] Detective Park.

425
00:23:23,424 --> 00:23:24,800
[♪ music increases in tempo]

426
00:23:35,602 --> 00:23:37,479
[♪ music swells, fades]

427
00:23:38,397 --> 00:23:39,398
[Isoo sighs softly]

428
00:23:39,481 --> 00:23:40,733
[cell phone vibrating]

429
00:23:43,277 --> 00:23:44,278
Hello, Dr. Yoon.

430
00:23:44,361 --> 00:23:46,363
The victim didn't burn to death.

431
00:23:46,947 --> 00:23:49,700
There's no soot in his trachea or bronchi.

432
00:23:49,783 --> 00:23:50,784
Then...

433
00:23:50,868 --> 00:23:52,161
[♪ tense, ticking music playing]

434
00:23:52,244 --> 00:23:55,831
He was already dead before the fire.

435
00:23:58,333 --> 00:24:00,210
-[line disconnects]
-What is it?

436
00:24:01,962 --> 00:24:03,922
He was already dead before the fire.

437
00:24:06,425 --> 00:24:07,426
[Kyungjin] Detective Joo!

438
00:24:08,260 --> 00:24:10,220
[♪ upbeat rock music playing]

439
00:24:10,304 --> 00:24:11,889
[panting] It's the same size
as the casket.

440
00:24:11,972 --> 00:24:13,348
And it smells of kerosene.

441
00:24:17,728 --> 00:24:19,354
It wasn't Park Jaeha.

442
00:24:19,438 --> 00:24:21,065
Park Jaehyung is the one who died.

443
00:24:21,148 --> 00:24:22,441
[scoffs incredulously]

444
00:24:26,028 --> 00:24:28,072
The one who had to disappear
was Park Jaeha.

445
00:24:28,155 --> 00:24:30,282
So he vanishes in the middle of his act?

446
00:24:31,617 --> 00:24:34,036
He kills Park Jaehyung
and puts him inside the casket.

447
00:24:34,703 --> 00:24:35,704
[thuds]

448
00:24:40,501 --> 00:24:42,127
[Isoo] Then he disappears
during the show...

449
00:24:44,046 --> 00:24:45,089
[flames whooshing]

450
00:24:47,883 --> 00:24:49,426
Making Park Jaeha the victim.

451
00:24:49,510 --> 00:24:51,386
Because they're twins.

452
00:24:51,470 --> 00:24:52,930
This is basically teleportation.

453
00:24:53,764 --> 00:24:55,140
We just need his fingerprint.

454
00:24:55,724 --> 00:24:56,725
Let's go.

455
00:24:58,685 --> 00:24:59,728
[♪ music fades]
STYLE
::cue()

456
00:25:03,690 --> 00:25:04,691
[exhales softly]

457
00:25:08,487 --> 00:25:09,696
Mr. Park Jaeha!

458
00:25:11,782 --> 00:25:12,825
Mr. Park Jaehyung!

459
00:25:14,493 --> 00:25:15,994
There you are.

460
00:25:16,745 --> 00:25:17,746
What were you up to?

461
00:25:17,830 --> 00:25:19,289
I have to clear this place out.

462
00:25:19,373 --> 00:25:22,626
-Oh, that's a lot of work. Let me help.
-No, it's all right.

463
00:25:22,709 --> 00:25:24,253
[♪ dramatic spy music playing]

464
00:25:24,336 --> 00:25:25,879
I'm going to take my time.

465
00:25:25,963 --> 00:25:28,132
[Isoo] You shouldn't push yourself
in your condition.

466
00:25:28,841 --> 00:25:30,717
-Shall I pack this?
-Don't touch...

467
00:25:33,846 --> 00:25:34,847
[in English] Magic.

468
00:25:34,930 --> 00:25:36,265
Magic...

469
00:25:36,348 --> 00:25:39,059
[in Korean] Did it disappear?
How did this...

470
00:25:39,143 --> 00:25:40,561
Jin Isoo.

471
00:25:40,644 --> 00:25:42,104
Stop bothering him and let's go.

472
00:25:42,771 --> 00:25:43,939
Sorry to bother you.

473
00:25:44,898 --> 00:25:45,899
Jeez.

474
00:25:45,983 --> 00:25:48,318
Let us know if you need any help.

475
00:25:48,402 --> 00:25:50,612
Anything, anytime. Detective Jin.

476
00:25:51,822 --> 00:25:52,990
[Jaehyung, softly] Goodness.

477
00:25:59,913 --> 00:26:01,748
[♪ music increases in tempo]

478
00:26:02,374 --> 00:26:03,584
Sir!

479
00:26:05,002 --> 00:26:06,378
We need fingerprints.

480
00:26:06,461 --> 00:26:07,713
[Kyungjin] It's urgent.

481
00:26:08,172 --> 00:26:09,423
[♪ music fades]

482
00:26:09,506 --> 00:26:12,009
[Hyera] He kept up the wheelchair act
even with no one around.

483
00:26:12,092 --> 00:26:14,887
He's very meticulous.

484
00:26:14,970 --> 00:26:16,471
We were really in sync just now.

485
00:26:16,555 --> 00:26:19,433
[chuckles] Yeah,
your acting is pretty good.

486
00:26:19,516 --> 00:26:22,352
[exhales smugly]
I'm just too talented for my own good.

487
00:26:23,437 --> 00:26:26,815
[sighs heavily]
Anyway, I've never seen a case like this.

488
00:26:27,691 --> 00:26:29,818
He killed his own brother to disappear.

489
00:26:30,819 --> 00:26:33,071
Let's get him
the second we get his fingerprints.

490
00:26:33,155 --> 00:26:34,531
I'll be the one to cuff him.

491
00:26:34,615 --> 00:26:36,116
[chuckles softly] Sure.

492
00:26:37,492 --> 00:26:39,453
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

493
00:26:41,914 --> 00:26:42,998
[tape ripping]

494
00:26:54,843 --> 00:26:56,261
[♪ music increases in tempo]

495
00:27:03,268 --> 00:27:04,269
[♪ music fades]

496
00:27:04,353 --> 00:27:05,687
-[cell phone vibrating]
-[Isoo sighs]

497
00:27:10,943 --> 00:27:12,152
-[Junyoung] Detective Joo.
-Yes?

498
00:27:12,236 --> 00:27:13,820
We didn't find any fingerprints.

499
00:27:14,404 --> 00:27:15,530
Huh?

500
00:27:15,614 --> 00:27:18,492
They say he would've suffered burns
while working with fire.

501
00:27:19,117 --> 00:27:20,994
We'll see if there are any other ways.

502
00:27:21,078 --> 00:27:22,746
Okay, got it.

503
00:27:22,829 --> 00:27:23,997
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

504
00:27:24,081 --> 00:27:25,916
He was packing a passport earlier.

505
00:27:25,999 --> 00:27:27,668
If he bolts, we'll never catch him.

506
00:27:28,377 --> 00:27:29,461
[sighs in exasperation]

507
00:27:29,544 --> 00:27:31,380
We need a clever way to...

508
00:27:31,880 --> 00:27:33,298
[♪ bright musical sting]

509
00:27:33,382 --> 00:27:35,300
There is a clever way.

510
00:27:35,384 --> 00:27:37,010
[♪ jaunty, suspenseful music playing]

511
00:27:37,094 --> 00:27:38,095
Like what?

512
00:27:38,845 --> 00:27:40,597
Stay here and don't let him get away.

513
00:27:43,058 --> 00:27:45,978
I'll make him shout out
that he's Park Jaeha.

514
00:27:46,061 --> 00:27:47,229
Jin Isoo!

515
00:27:49,106 --> 00:27:50,440
-[sighs softly]
-[♪ music fades]

516
00:27:51,066 --> 00:27:52,734
Why did he suddenly call for us?

517
00:27:53,986 --> 00:27:55,487
-You're all here!
-Hello.

518
00:27:55,570 --> 00:27:56,822
What a relief.

519
00:27:57,447 --> 00:27:58,949
-It's been a while.
-Yes, sir.

520
00:27:59,074 --> 00:28:01,493
I have an urgent project.

521
00:28:01,576 --> 00:28:03,704
What's the name
of that movie we're working on?

522
00:28:03,787 --> 00:28:05,956
The End of Humanity.

523
00:28:06,039 --> 00:28:08,625
Let's rehearse Scene 27.

524
00:28:08,709 --> 00:28:09,710
Right now.

525
00:28:09,793 --> 00:28:11,378
[♪ upbeat rock music playing]

526
00:28:18,135 --> 00:28:19,219
[tires screech]

527
00:28:19,761 --> 00:28:21,221
[tires screech]

528
00:28:25,726 --> 00:28:26,852
ISCG INFECTION CONTROL

529
00:28:34,860 --> 00:28:36,403
[♪ upbeat rock music continues]
STYLE
::cue()

530
00:28:47,664 --> 00:28:51,001
PROJECT ISCG:
THE END OF HUMANITY

531
00:28:51,084 --> 00:28:52,127
[♪ music fades]

532
00:28:54,755 --> 00:28:55,756
[grunts softly]

533
00:28:56,882 --> 00:28:57,883
[exhales softly]

534
00:28:59,760 --> 00:29:00,761
[sighs deeply]

535
00:29:03,722 --> 00:29:05,557
Time to say goodbye to this place.

536
00:29:06,141 --> 00:29:07,309
[scoffs softly]

537
00:29:09,352 --> 00:29:10,604
[Isoo] Mr. Park Jaehyung.

538
00:29:10,687 --> 00:29:12,898
Mr. Park Jaehyung! Where are you?

539
00:29:12,981 --> 00:29:14,608
Ah! Are you Park Jaehyung?

540
00:29:14,691 --> 00:29:16,526
Yes, I am.

541
00:29:16,610 --> 00:29:18,320
-[♪ quirky, dramatic music playing]
-[sprayers hissing]

542
00:29:18,403 --> 00:29:20,822
[Isoo] Did you have blood tests done
at Munsan Hospital?

543
00:29:21,823 --> 00:29:25,452
A deadly, contagious virus
was found in your blood.

544
00:29:25,869 --> 00:29:26,870
What?

545
00:29:26,953 --> 00:29:29,289
[Isoo] This is a virus
that's never been identified before.

546
00:29:29,372 --> 00:29:30,791
If this gets out...

547
00:29:31,666 --> 00:29:33,001
it's the end of humanity.

548
00:29:33,418 --> 00:29:34,419
What?

549
00:29:35,212 --> 00:29:37,255
[Kyungjin] It looks like
the virus is only in here!

550
00:29:37,339 --> 00:29:38,799
It hasn't spread outside.

551
00:29:38,882 --> 00:29:41,551
[Junyoung] We must kill the host
and burn this whole place down!

552
00:29:41,968 --> 00:29:43,303
[Isoo] Let's take him to the lab.

553
00:29:43,386 --> 00:29:45,430
[Kyungjin] What if more people
get infected?

554
00:29:45,514 --> 00:29:48,058
Tens of thousands could die
before we have a vaccine!

555
00:29:48,141 --> 00:29:49,726
[Junyoung mutters, grunts]

556
00:29:49,810 --> 00:29:51,895
[gasps] Wait, hold on!

557
00:29:51,978 --> 00:29:53,605
[Junyoung] We must kill him here!

558
00:29:54,648 --> 00:29:57,359
[Isoo, sighs] Is this truly the only way?

559
00:29:57,442 --> 00:29:59,528
[Kyungjin] If we keep quiet,
we can stop a catastrophe.

560
00:30:00,529 --> 00:30:02,155
[Junyoung] I'll take responsibility.

561
00:30:05,033 --> 00:30:06,118
[Isoo] Mr. Park Jaehyung.

562
00:30:07,119 --> 00:30:08,120
We're sorry.

563
00:30:09,287 --> 00:30:10,914
Your sacrifice will save humanity.

564
00:30:10,997 --> 00:30:12,207
What?

565
00:30:12,290 --> 00:30:15,085
[Isoo] You are our hero,
Mr. Park Jaehyung.

566
00:30:15,168 --> 00:30:16,336
[Kyungjin, in English] Hero.

567
00:30:19,464 --> 00:30:20,966
[Isoo, in Korean] We promise

568
00:30:21,466 --> 00:30:22,467
to remember you.

569
00:30:22,551 --> 00:30:23,844
Shoot him.

570
00:30:23,927 --> 00:30:26,388
-[Junyoung grunts]
-Wait! Please, wait.

571
00:30:26,471 --> 00:30:27,472
Wait.

572
00:30:29,808 --> 00:30:30,809
I'm...

573
00:30:31,810 --> 00:30:33,019
not Park Jaehyung.

574
00:30:33,103 --> 00:30:35,313
[Isoo] Do not be afraid of death.
Shoot him.

575
00:30:35,397 --> 00:30:36,606
-[Junyoung grunts]
-[Jaehyung] Wait, please!

576
00:30:36,690 --> 00:30:37,774
Wait.

577
00:30:37,858 --> 00:30:38,859
I'm...

578
00:30:39,776 --> 00:30:41,069
not Park Jaehyung.

579
00:30:41,153 --> 00:30:42,529
I'm Park Jaeha, his brother!

580
00:30:42,612 --> 00:30:45,073
[Isoo] Mr. Park Jaeha died a few days ago.

581
00:30:45,157 --> 00:30:47,075
-[Junyoung grunts]
-Wait, stop!

582
00:30:47,784 --> 00:30:48,785
I'm...

583
00:30:48,869 --> 00:30:50,912
I'm the magician, Park Jaeha!

584
00:30:50,996 --> 00:30:52,706
-Look!
-[all exclaim in disbelief]

585
00:30:52,789 --> 00:30:54,791
[Jaeha] Look.

586
00:30:54,875 --> 00:30:57,419
My brother couldn't walk
after his accident, but look.

587
00:30:57,502 --> 00:30:58,962
Park Jaeha's magic fire!

588
00:30:59,045 --> 00:31:01,756
The waltz.

589
00:31:01,840 --> 00:31:02,841
Look. See?

590
00:31:02,924 --> 00:31:04,718
I'm light on my feet! See that?

591
00:31:04,801 --> 00:31:05,886
-Right?
-[Isoo, in English] What the...

592
00:31:05,969 --> 00:31:08,054
[in Korean] I'm Jaeha!

593
00:31:08,138 --> 00:31:09,764
[Isoo, in English] Oh, my God.

594
00:31:09,848 --> 00:31:10,849
[in Korean] Who?

595
00:31:10,932 --> 00:31:13,351
Park Jaeha!

596
00:31:13,435 --> 00:31:14,436
[Kyungjin] Wow.

597
00:31:15,103 --> 00:31:16,438
[Isoo scoffs incredulously]

598
00:31:16,521 --> 00:31:17,564
[in English] Jesus.

599
00:31:17,647 --> 00:31:18,815
[in Korean] Park Jaeha.

600
00:31:18,899 --> 00:31:20,901
Huh? Huh?

601
00:31:21,693 --> 00:31:23,403
You said you're Park Jaeha, right?

602
00:31:23,486 --> 00:31:25,197
[♪ upbeat swing jazz music playing]

603
00:31:26,031 --> 00:31:27,032
Park Jaeha.

604
00:31:27,616 --> 00:31:30,118
You're under arrest
for the murder of Park Jaehyung.

605
00:31:30,202 --> 00:31:31,328
[handcuffs clicking]

606
00:31:34,289 --> 00:31:35,498
[exhales heavily]

607
00:31:36,208 --> 00:31:37,209
[sighs softly]

608
00:31:37,751 --> 00:31:38,877
[exclaims smugly]

609
00:31:40,086 --> 00:31:42,505
You're pretty startled
for a magician, huh?

610
00:31:42,589 --> 00:31:43,673
[in English] Surprise!

611
00:31:43,757 --> 00:31:45,967
That virus...

612
00:31:46,051 --> 00:31:47,260
[in Korean] It's a trick.

613
00:31:47,344 --> 00:31:49,471
A show just for Park Jaeha.

614
00:31:50,305 --> 00:31:51,306
[yelps]

615
00:31:52,182 --> 00:31:53,558
[whimpers, gasps]

616
00:31:59,397 --> 00:32:00,482
[softly] What?

617
00:32:00,941 --> 00:32:01,942
[exhales incredulously]

618
00:32:02,025 --> 00:32:03,026
What on earth?

619
00:32:05,528 --> 00:32:08,198
What's ISCG?
It's not part of the police, is it?

620
00:32:08,281 --> 00:32:09,658
[Isoo] This?

621
00:32:12,869 --> 00:32:15,330
ISOO COOL GUY

622
00:32:15,413 --> 00:32:16,414
[♪ music fades]
STYLE
::cue()

623
00:32:16,498 --> 00:32:18,416
SEOUL GANGHA POLICE STATION

624
00:32:20,377 --> 00:32:22,128
Tell us what happened.

625
00:32:23,171 --> 00:32:24,965
Sujeong's dad

626
00:32:25,882 --> 00:32:28,009
sent his men to take me to him.

627
00:32:28,093 --> 00:32:29,219
[Seongwook] Your hand

628
00:32:30,387 --> 00:32:31,513
is mine.

629
00:32:31,596 --> 00:32:32,973
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

630
00:32:36,685 --> 00:32:37,894
Cut it off.

631
00:32:41,314 --> 00:32:42,315
Wait.

632
00:32:44,818 --> 00:32:45,819
Aren't you afraid?

633
00:32:45,902 --> 00:32:47,362
The only thing I'm afraid of...

634
00:32:48,071 --> 00:32:50,115
is not keeping my promise to the audience.

635
00:32:51,533 --> 00:32:52,826
It's a shame. [sighs]

636
00:32:53,702 --> 00:32:56,162
I'd hoped a man like you
would become my son-in-law.

637
00:32:58,290 --> 00:33:00,250
That's not what we heard.

638
00:33:01,543 --> 00:33:02,627
[sighs regretfully]

639
00:33:03,753 --> 00:33:05,088
So I told him.

640
00:33:08,466 --> 00:33:10,093
Once I finish my final performance,

641
00:33:11,261 --> 00:33:13,346
I will come back here on my own. And then,

642
00:33:14,347 --> 00:33:15,557
you can take my hand.

643
00:33:18,226 --> 00:33:19,602
Did you really mean that?

644
00:33:19,686 --> 00:33:22,647
-[♪ music fades]
-No. In all honesty,

645
00:33:24,691 --> 00:33:25,734
I just couldn't do it.

646
00:33:25,817 --> 00:33:28,528
How can a magician live without his hands?
Huh?

647
00:33:30,071 --> 00:33:32,907
I spent all day thinking it over,

648
00:33:35,618 --> 00:33:37,037
then I went to see my brother.

649
00:33:37,120 --> 00:33:38,496
[♪ foreboding music playing]

650
00:33:39,122 --> 00:33:41,416
Because I need money to run away.

651
00:33:46,004 --> 00:33:47,005
Jaehyung.

652
00:33:49,841 --> 00:33:50,842
Jaehyung.

653
00:33:57,265 --> 00:33:58,266
[gasps softly]

654
00:33:59,059 --> 00:34:00,060
Jaehyung.

655
00:34:02,312 --> 00:34:03,730
ORAL MEDICATION

656
00:34:05,106 --> 00:34:06,191
[breath trembles]

657
00:34:08,735 --> 00:34:09,944
But

658
00:34:11,112 --> 00:34:12,447
he was dead.

659
00:34:12,530 --> 00:34:13,907
[♪ music swells, fades]

660
00:34:13,990 --> 00:34:15,033
[Isoo] Hey.

661
00:34:15,867 --> 00:34:17,535
If you lie, we'll know.

662
00:34:18,161 --> 00:34:20,038
[frantically] I'm not lying.
It's the truth.

663
00:34:20,121 --> 00:34:22,707
I promise. I even have his suicide note.

664
00:34:22,791 --> 00:34:24,501
[exhales sharply] I promise.

665
00:34:24,584 --> 00:34:26,294
Anyway... [breath trembling]

666
00:34:26,378 --> 00:34:28,004
...I knew he had cancer,

667
00:34:28,671 --> 00:34:31,299
but I didn't know it was that serious.

668
00:34:31,383 --> 00:34:33,760
It seems there was no way to treat it.

669
00:34:34,511 --> 00:34:35,804
So then what did you do?

670
00:34:35,887 --> 00:34:37,013
At first...

671
00:34:37,097 --> 00:34:38,640
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

672
00:34:38,723 --> 00:34:40,183
...I was really shaken up...

673
00:34:40,266 --> 00:34:41,768
[breathing heavily]

674
00:34:47,148 --> 00:34:49,275
but then I thought,

675
00:34:50,527 --> 00:34:52,487
"I really am lucky."

676
00:34:53,196 --> 00:34:55,156
We're twins,

677
00:34:55,240 --> 00:34:57,575
so it's the perfect way to disappear.
[chuckles]

678
00:34:58,910 --> 00:35:01,788
Oh. So,

679
00:35:01,871 --> 00:35:05,083
your brother died,
but you came up with that perfect plan?

680
00:35:05,166 --> 00:35:06,292
[sighs]

681
00:35:06,376 --> 00:35:07,836
He was already dead,

682
00:35:08,920 --> 00:35:11,464
so I thought he was
helping me until the very end.

683
00:35:11,548 --> 00:35:13,049
[♪ gripping, foreboding music playing]

684
00:35:16,386 --> 00:35:17,762
FAREWELL NOTE

685
00:35:17,846 --> 00:35:19,305
DAILY LIFE WAS PAINFUL

686
00:35:19,389 --> 00:35:21,141
THANK YOU ALL FOR EVERYTHING

687
00:35:29,649 --> 00:35:31,484
[♪ music increases in tempo]
STYLE
::cue()

688
00:36:06,978 --> 00:36:08,605
[♪ music slows, fades]

689
00:36:08,688 --> 00:36:09,939
Jaeha.

690
00:36:10,023 --> 00:36:11,191
Hey, Luna.

691
00:36:12,025 --> 00:36:14,569
I had a really scary dream today.

692
00:36:15,320 --> 00:36:16,321
What kind of dream?

693
00:36:17,405 --> 00:36:19,073
A dream about you dying.

694
00:36:19,783 --> 00:36:20,909
Ah.

695
00:36:21,576 --> 00:36:23,578
Can't you skip today's show?

696
00:36:23,661 --> 00:36:25,246
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

697
00:36:28,041 --> 00:36:30,585
I have to treat it
like my last performance

698
00:36:30,668 --> 00:36:32,295
and do my best.

699
00:36:40,553 --> 00:36:41,638
[gunshot]

700
00:36:42,013 --> 00:36:43,223
[♪ music increases in tempo]

701
00:37:06,996 --> 00:37:08,289
[fire roaring]

702
00:37:08,373 --> 00:37:09,916
-[burning wood crashes]
-[Dahee screams]

703
00:37:09,999 --> 00:37:11,626
[screaming in horror]

704
00:37:11,709 --> 00:37:13,211
[audience exclaiming in horror]

705
00:37:14,128 --> 00:37:15,547
Get everyone to safety first.

706
00:37:15,630 --> 00:37:17,006
[clamoring]

707
00:37:23,137 --> 00:37:24,556
[♪ music fades]

708
00:37:24,639 --> 00:37:26,391
[♪ tense, foreboding music playing]

709
00:37:29,686 --> 00:37:31,062
[♪ music increases in tempo]

710
00:37:38,069 --> 00:37:39,696
[breathing heavily]

711
00:37:42,407 --> 00:37:43,658
[knock at door]

712
00:37:43,741 --> 00:37:45,785
[Isoo] Hello? This is the police.

713
00:37:52,000 --> 00:37:53,209
[switch clicks]

714
00:37:53,293 --> 00:37:54,586
[wheelchair whirs]

715
00:37:54,669 --> 00:37:55,795
[♪ music swells]

716
00:37:57,839 --> 00:37:58,882
[♪ music fades]

717
00:37:58,965 --> 00:38:01,175
So you burned your dead brother

718
00:38:01,259 --> 00:38:02,886
to disappear completely?

719
00:38:02,969 --> 00:38:05,930
Of course, I didn't feel good about it.

720
00:38:07,181 --> 00:38:09,267
But he was going to be cremated anyway.

721
00:38:09,350 --> 00:38:10,518
[sighs sarcastically]

722
00:38:12,854 --> 00:38:14,772
[exhales] I'm so touched.

723
00:38:15,690 --> 00:38:18,318
Is this what people call
the total package?

724
00:38:18,401 --> 00:38:20,945
Love life, family, colleagues,
performance, character.

725
00:38:21,029 --> 00:38:22,322
All completely trash.

726
00:38:22,947 --> 00:38:23,948
Trash?

727
00:38:24,032 --> 00:38:26,159
I've never met anyone so obnoxious before.

728
00:38:26,242 --> 00:38:27,410
[breathing heavily]

729
00:38:27,493 --> 00:38:29,120
[♪ quirky, dramatic music playing]

730
00:38:29,203 --> 00:38:30,246
What else could I do?

731
00:38:30,330 --> 00:38:31,497
I was scared.

732
00:38:31,581 --> 00:38:33,499
Ever had your hand go into a straw cutter?

733
00:38:33,583 --> 00:38:35,043
It's really sharp.

734
00:38:36,294 --> 00:38:38,796
Anyway, all I did

735
00:38:38,880 --> 00:38:41,049
was burn my brother's dead body,

736
00:38:41,841 --> 00:38:45,053
so is there any chance
I could get a suspended sentence?

737
00:38:47,013 --> 00:38:48,014
Isoo Cool Guy.

738
00:38:49,223 --> 00:38:50,308
Uncross your fingers.

739
00:38:51,684 --> 00:38:53,603
Suspended sentence, my ass.

740
00:38:54,520 --> 00:38:57,065
You think the judges are
crazy enough to do that, huh?

741
00:38:57,148 --> 00:38:58,483
What's the matter with you?

742
00:38:59,651 --> 00:39:00,985
Aren't you being a bit harsh?

743
00:39:01,069 --> 00:39:02,612
-Come here.
-[exclaims]

744
00:39:02,695 --> 00:39:03,696
[♪ music fades]

745
00:39:03,780 --> 00:39:05,073
Jaeha's alive?

746
00:39:05,156 --> 00:39:06,783
Yes. Uh...

747
00:39:06,866 --> 00:39:09,202
He used his dead brother
so he could run away.

748
00:39:09,285 --> 00:39:11,162
Huh? That's so creepy.

749
00:39:11,788 --> 00:39:13,498
Then the dream I had...

750
00:39:13,581 --> 00:39:15,875
Mmm, it was about Park Jaehyung.

751
00:39:15,959 --> 00:39:17,794
I guess you really can see the future.

752
00:39:17,877 --> 00:39:19,170
[Jiyun sighs]

753
00:39:19,253 --> 00:39:22,173
I can't believe the person I loved
was that messed up.

754
00:39:22,256 --> 00:39:24,968
[sighs deeply] I know how you feel.

755
00:39:25,051 --> 00:39:26,678
I always fall for the bad women.

756
00:39:26,761 --> 00:39:28,471
-I wonder why.
-[Jiyun scoffs softly]

757
00:39:29,472 --> 00:39:32,809
Actually, Waiter Hong!
Give us your most expensive whiskey.

758
00:39:32,892 --> 00:39:34,394
No, a drink to celebrate.
STYLE
::cue()

759
00:39:34,477 --> 00:39:36,145
Give us a bottle of champagne.

760
00:39:36,229 --> 00:39:37,271
[Jiyun scoffs softly]

761
00:39:37,355 --> 00:39:39,065
[♪ upbeat, jaunty music playing]

762
00:39:41,901 --> 00:39:43,194
Now,

763
00:39:43,277 --> 00:39:45,738
you're finally free
from that piece of trash,

764
00:39:45,822 --> 00:39:47,699
so here's to your new life.

765
00:39:48,700 --> 00:39:49,867
-[clinking]
-Cheers.

766
00:39:54,038 --> 00:39:55,164
Mmm.

767
00:39:55,498 --> 00:39:56,582
[sighs in exasperation]

768
00:39:56,666 --> 00:40:00,044
I really don't think I'll feel any better
until I punch that bastard.

769
00:40:00,128 --> 00:40:01,379
Mmm...

770
00:40:02,296 --> 00:40:04,132
[in English] Good idea.
[in Korean] I like it.

771
00:40:05,466 --> 00:40:06,718
Yes, cheers again.

772
00:40:07,301 --> 00:40:08,386
[clinking]

773
00:40:08,845 --> 00:40:10,179
[inhales sharply]

774
00:40:10,263 --> 00:40:11,431
[exhales softly]

775
00:40:11,514 --> 00:40:12,765
[♪ music fades]

776
00:40:13,725 --> 00:40:16,144
SEOUL GANGHA POLICE STATION

777
00:40:16,227 --> 00:40:18,396
Park Jaeha? I heard he's dead.

778
00:40:18,479 --> 00:40:19,939
What's a dead guy doing here?

779
00:40:20,023 --> 00:40:21,774
-Show us.
-Show us a magic trick.

780
00:40:21,858 --> 00:40:23,067
How can I do magic here?

781
00:40:23,151 --> 00:40:24,402
Do it.

782
00:40:24,485 --> 00:40:25,611
-Please stop.
-Do it.

783
00:40:25,695 --> 00:40:26,738
[Jaeha] Don't touch me.

784
00:40:27,864 --> 00:40:29,741
Oh, those guys are back again?

785
00:40:31,909 --> 00:40:33,703
-Did you need something?
-Ah.

786
00:40:34,579 --> 00:40:35,663
I need a word.

787
00:40:35,747 --> 00:40:37,623
[♪ quirky, suspenseful music playing]

788
00:40:40,418 --> 00:40:41,919
[whispering] We'll take
Park Jaeha out and...

789
00:40:42,003 --> 00:40:43,379
[continues indistinctly]

790
00:40:53,723 --> 00:40:54,891
Stop touching me.

791
00:40:54,974 --> 00:40:55,975
Do some magic for us.

792
00:40:58,186 --> 00:41:00,772
Mr. Park Jaeha,
you're being moved to jail. Come out.

793
00:41:00,855 --> 00:41:02,065
[chuckles in relief]

794
00:41:02,148 --> 00:41:03,775
-Show us before you go.
-Don't go.

795
00:41:07,945 --> 00:41:09,197
Go left.

796
00:41:09,864 --> 00:41:13,284
My God, you look terrible, Mr. Park.

797
00:41:13,993 --> 00:41:15,203
Come here.

798
00:41:15,286 --> 00:41:16,329
It's all right.

799
00:41:16,412 --> 00:41:18,372
[in English] Now, follow me.

800
00:41:22,960 --> 00:41:24,754
Oh! Oh...

801
00:41:24,837 --> 00:41:26,005
[♪ music fades]

802
00:41:27,256 --> 00:41:28,382
[chuckles nervously]

803
00:41:29,175 --> 00:41:31,094
[in Korean] Did you come to say goodbye?

804
00:41:31,177 --> 00:41:33,096
We couldn't just let you go.

805
00:41:34,472 --> 00:41:35,723
-You son of a bitch.
-What?

806
00:41:35,807 --> 00:41:36,974
[♪ quirky music playing]

807
00:41:37,058 --> 00:41:39,268
-You!
-You bastard! How could you?

808
00:41:39,352 --> 00:41:42,021
You shouldn't be doing this, ladies.
The stomach!

809
00:41:42,855 --> 00:41:45,399
-[officer] That's enough.
-[Dahee] Get out of the way.

810
00:41:45,483 --> 00:41:46,901
You bastard!

811
00:41:46,984 --> 00:41:48,194
[Jaeha] I...

812
00:41:48,277 --> 00:41:49,403
[Jiyun panting]

813
00:41:49,987 --> 00:41:51,322
I loved all of you.

814
00:41:54,951 --> 00:41:56,244
[exclaims]

815
00:41:56,327 --> 00:41:57,370
Shut your mouth.

816
00:41:58,329 --> 00:41:59,831
[Hyera] What's going on?

817
00:42:00,540 --> 00:42:03,376
Right. Isn't the transport van over there?

818
00:42:03,459 --> 00:42:04,710
I guess I was mistaken.

819
00:42:04,794 --> 00:42:06,212
What? It's at the front gate.

820
00:42:06,295 --> 00:42:08,047
It's the front gate. Ah, my mistake.

821
00:42:08,131 --> 00:42:09,132
Mistake?

822
00:42:09,215 --> 00:42:11,717
Yes, exactly. Nobody's perfect.

823
00:42:12,510 --> 00:42:13,970
Hey, take him away.

824
00:42:16,055 --> 00:42:17,598
[Jaeha] I really loved you.

825
00:42:17,682 --> 00:42:18,933
-I mean it.
-Bro.

826
00:42:20,101 --> 00:42:21,936
Well done. Time to go home.

827
00:42:22,019 --> 00:42:24,564
You've got a mean punch.
Ever thought about boxing?

828
00:42:24,647 --> 00:42:25,815
Jin Isoo.

829
00:42:26,440 --> 00:42:28,985
-Submit a written apology.
-A written apology.

830
00:42:29,068 --> 00:42:31,654
That's my specialty. You got it.

831
00:42:31,737 --> 00:42:33,698
-[scoffs]
-[♪ music fades]
STYLE
::cue()

832
00:42:38,870 --> 00:42:40,538
[sneezing]

833
00:42:42,415 --> 00:42:43,457
[door opens]

834
00:42:47,211 --> 00:42:48,379
[Jaeha sighs softly]

835
00:42:48,462 --> 00:42:50,756
[♪ gentle, wistful music playing]

836
00:42:50,840 --> 00:42:52,049
Sujeong.

837
00:43:08,524 --> 00:43:09,525
Sujeong.

838
00:43:10,568 --> 00:43:11,694
[chuckles]

839
00:43:11,777 --> 00:43:13,154
My Sujeong.

840
00:43:14,739 --> 00:43:16,115
You look beautiful today.

841
00:43:17,533 --> 00:43:19,493
Like a cherry blossom. [chuckling]

842
00:43:20,703 --> 00:43:21,954
[sighs softly]

843
00:43:23,289 --> 00:43:25,249
Did you come all the way here to see me?

844
00:43:26,959 --> 00:43:27,960
Jaeha.

845
00:43:29,003 --> 00:43:30,546
You'll be out of here soon.

846
00:43:31,464 --> 00:43:34,634
My dad hired a great lawyer.

847
00:43:40,598 --> 00:43:41,724
[exhales sharply]

848
00:43:43,809 --> 00:43:45,811
[voice shaking] I don't know
what I'd do without you.

849
00:43:49,065 --> 00:43:51,150
You were my first love.

850
00:43:53,486 --> 00:43:54,487
But...

851
00:43:54,570 --> 00:43:57,406
[inhales deeply, exhales]

852
00:43:57,490 --> 00:43:59,742
...my life feels meaningless now.

853
00:43:59,825 --> 00:44:00,993
[breath trembles]

854
00:44:03,871 --> 00:44:05,039
I'll make it up to you.

855
00:44:05,748 --> 00:44:06,916
From now on,

856
00:44:07,959 --> 00:44:09,543
I'll be really good to you.

857
00:44:11,379 --> 00:44:13,089
You should.

858
00:44:13,172 --> 00:44:15,716
I'll be spending every day
waiting for you to get out.

859
00:44:15,800 --> 00:44:16,968
[♪ music fades]

860
00:44:19,053 --> 00:44:20,221
Once you're out,

861
00:44:21,889 --> 00:44:23,599
I'm going to kill you myself.

862
00:44:23,683 --> 00:44:25,768
[♪ tense, foreboding music playing]

863
00:44:28,229 --> 00:44:29,313
[chuckling nervously]

864
00:44:32,525 --> 00:44:35,528
Why would you say
something so scary, Sujeong?

865
00:44:36,070 --> 00:44:38,906
Try running if you want.

866
00:44:38,990 --> 00:44:40,700
Wherever you hide,

867
00:44:41,659 --> 00:44:43,077
I'm going to find you.

868
00:44:43,160 --> 00:44:44,954
-[♪ music fades]
-What?

869
00:44:46,330 --> 00:44:48,124
All the best until then.

870
00:44:48,207 --> 00:44:49,417
[♪ quirky music playing]

871
00:44:49,500 --> 00:44:50,835
Wait, Sujeong.

872
00:44:50,918 --> 00:44:51,919
Sujeong!

873
00:44:52,837 --> 00:44:54,046
Sujeong, wait!

874
00:44:55,172 --> 00:44:56,882
You've suddenly changed!

875
00:44:56,966 --> 00:44:58,426
Why are you doing this to me?

876
00:44:59,302 --> 00:45:01,429
[voice shaking] If you do this too,
what am I supposed to do?

877
00:45:01,512 --> 00:45:02,680
[sobbing]

878
00:45:04,390 --> 00:45:05,474
[♪ music fades]

879
00:45:11,230 --> 00:45:12,773
[line ringing over car speaker]

880
00:45:13,816 --> 00:45:16,485
[automated voice] The number
you have dialed is unavailable.

881
00:45:16,569 --> 00:45:18,529
Why isn't he picking up?

882
00:45:19,530 --> 00:45:21,490
MR. CHOI

883
00:45:22,825 --> 00:45:24,785
[line connects, ringing]

884
00:45:26,287 --> 00:45:28,456
-Yes, Detective Jin.
-Hi, Mr. Kim.

885
00:45:29,123 --> 00:45:32,293
I can't seem to reach the chairman lately.
Is he very busy?

886
00:45:32,376 --> 00:45:34,003
He's on vacation.

887
00:45:35,087 --> 00:45:37,381
-Vacation?
-He didn't say he was traveling.

888
00:45:37,465 --> 00:45:39,550
-Shall I call him for you?
-No, it's fine.

889
00:45:39,633 --> 00:45:41,844
He'll be reading books at home, then.

890
00:45:41,927 --> 00:45:44,263
That's his idea of a vacation.
I'll go to his house.

891
00:45:44,347 --> 00:45:45,639
[engine revving]

892
00:45:52,646 --> 00:45:53,981
[doorbell chimes]

893
00:45:56,025 --> 00:45:57,401
[doorbell chimes]

894
00:45:58,903 --> 00:45:59,904
What on earth?

895
00:46:01,238 --> 00:46:02,823
-[door unlocks]
-[digital lock beeps]

896
00:46:02,907 --> 00:46:05,076
-[door closes]
-Mr. Choi, it's me!

897
00:46:05,159 --> 00:46:06,202
[digital lock beeps]

898
00:46:08,162 --> 00:46:09,288
Mr. Choi!

899
00:46:12,333 --> 00:46:14,001
PRE AND POST STOMACH CANCER SURGERY

900
00:46:20,424 --> 00:46:21,675
PRE-SURGERY PREPARATION

901
00:46:21,759 --> 00:46:23,010
[♪ gentle, melancholy music playing]

902
00:46:23,886 --> 00:46:26,097
ADMISSION INFORMATION

903
00:46:36,315 --> 00:46:37,441
[sighs softly]

904
00:46:46,992 --> 00:46:48,285
What are you doing here?

905
00:46:48,369 --> 00:46:49,662
Detective Jin.

906
00:46:53,374 --> 00:46:55,084
I asked, what are you doing?

907
00:46:55,751 --> 00:46:57,128
How did you know I was here?
STYLE
::cue()

908
00:47:00,131 --> 00:47:01,215
[Isoo sighs]

909
00:47:01,298 --> 00:47:02,758
Were you never going to tell me?

910
00:47:03,634 --> 00:47:05,469
It's not a serious illness.

911
00:47:05,553 --> 00:47:07,221
And the surgery went well.

912
00:47:09,682 --> 00:47:12,226
I thought of you as family.

913
00:47:13,561 --> 00:47:15,479
But it looks like I meant nothing to you.

914
00:47:16,313 --> 00:47:18,315
I just didn't want to bother you.

915
00:47:20,025 --> 00:47:21,026
Did I scare you?

916
00:47:21,110 --> 00:47:22,111
[sighs softly]

917
00:47:23,112 --> 00:47:25,281
In my recent case,

918
00:47:25,364 --> 00:47:27,450
a terminal cancer patient
took his own life.

919
00:47:28,659 --> 00:47:30,536
But then I hear that you have cancer.

920
00:47:32,621 --> 00:47:33,831
[sighs heavily]

921
00:47:35,833 --> 00:47:36,876
I'm sorry.

922
00:47:37,793 --> 00:47:38,794
[Isoo sighs softly]

923
00:47:39,879 --> 00:47:40,880
[♪ music fades]

924
00:47:46,552 --> 00:47:47,595
[Isoo sighs]

925
00:47:49,430 --> 00:47:51,432
Why is your hospital room so shabby?

926
00:47:51,515 --> 00:47:54,810
It's not shabby at all.
It's a perfectly nice room.

927
00:47:54,894 --> 00:47:56,353
You don't even have any flowers.

928
00:47:56,437 --> 00:47:58,689
I don't need flowers at my age. [chuckles]

929
00:47:59,523 --> 00:48:01,150
And your clothes are all wet.

930
00:48:01,233 --> 00:48:03,110
How are you going to get changed, huh?

931
00:48:03,194 --> 00:48:05,779
As if you'd bother me.
Take it off and change.

932
00:48:05,863 --> 00:48:08,574
I'll do it myself later.

933
00:48:08,657 --> 00:48:10,159
[inhales sharply] Take it off.
You need to change!

934
00:48:10,242 --> 00:48:11,410
Uh... [exhales]

935
00:48:11,494 --> 00:48:13,245
[♪ gentle, poignant music playing]

936
00:48:13,329 --> 00:48:14,413
[grunts softly]

937
00:48:19,001 --> 00:48:20,753
GET WELL SOON

938
00:48:21,378 --> 00:48:22,379
Thank you.

939
00:48:25,925 --> 00:48:27,051
[door opens]

940
00:48:28,552 --> 00:48:29,595
[door closes]

941
00:48:32,806 --> 00:48:34,016
[sneezes]

942
00:48:37,102 --> 00:48:38,562
Whoa!

943
00:48:39,813 --> 00:48:41,607
-Looks like someone was here.
-[coughs]

944
00:48:41,690 --> 00:48:42,775
Yes.

945
00:48:43,317 --> 00:48:45,277
Someone I think of as a son stopped by.

946
00:48:45,361 --> 00:48:46,695
[chuckles]

947
00:48:46,779 --> 00:48:49,240
The scent's quite strong.

948
00:48:49,323 --> 00:48:51,116
It is. [sneezes]

949
00:48:51,200 --> 00:48:52,326
[chuckling]

950
00:48:52,409 --> 00:48:53,953
[exhales sharply]

951
00:48:54,036 --> 00:48:55,621
[panting]

952
00:48:55,704 --> 00:48:56,747
[♪ music fades]

953
00:49:00,251 --> 00:49:01,418
[cell phone vibrating]

954
00:49:05,214 --> 00:49:06,215
Hey, babe.

955
00:49:07,049 --> 00:49:08,050
[Kyungjin gasps]

956
00:49:08,509 --> 00:49:09,510
[whispering] Shoot, I forgot.

957
00:49:09,593 --> 00:49:12,429
Okay, I'll be right there. Sorry.

958
00:49:13,514 --> 00:49:14,515
[line disconnects]

959
00:49:15,224 --> 00:49:17,393
Hey, where are you going?

960
00:49:17,476 --> 00:49:18,686
To see my girlfriend.

961
00:49:18,769 --> 00:49:20,813
We're supposed to hang out today.

962
00:49:20,896 --> 00:49:23,607
I forgot I had a date. Sorry, bro!

963
00:49:23,691 --> 00:49:24,942
Hey!

964
00:49:25,818 --> 00:49:27,027
[sighs]

965
00:49:27,111 --> 00:49:29,113
He's completely whipped by his girlfriend.

966
00:49:29,196 --> 00:49:31,073
-[sighs in exasperation]
-[cell phone vibrating]

967
00:49:35,411 --> 00:49:36,870
Hi, Jiwon.

968
00:49:38,163 --> 00:49:39,957
What? Where are you?

969
00:49:40,040 --> 00:49:42,376
I'll be right there. I won't be long.

970
00:49:42,459 --> 00:49:43,961
-[line disconnects]
-Hey, what's going on?

971
00:49:44,044 --> 00:49:45,170
Jiwon hurt herself.

972
00:49:45,254 --> 00:49:46,880
I need to go. Sorry. Bye.

973
00:49:46,964 --> 00:49:47,965
Hey, you're...

974
00:49:48,048 --> 00:49:49,174
[♪ quirky music playing]

975
00:49:50,593 --> 00:49:52,136
He's the one who's whipped.

976
00:49:53,262 --> 00:49:54,722
[exhales incredulously]

977
00:49:56,307 --> 00:49:57,391
[clicks tongue]

978
00:50:01,020 --> 00:50:02,438
[line connects, ringing]

979
00:50:04,607 --> 00:50:06,984
-[line clicks]
-Hello? Yes, it's me.

980
00:50:07,067 --> 00:50:10,946
I can't make it today,
so I'll have to cancel.

981
00:50:11,864 --> 00:50:12,990
[line disconnects]

982
00:50:13,073 --> 00:50:16,076
Where is everyone? I thought
you were having a guys-only party.

983
00:50:16,160 --> 00:50:17,578
They betrayed me.

984
00:50:19,538 --> 00:50:20,914
[keyboard clacking]

985
00:50:22,666 --> 00:50:23,834
[♪ music fades]

986
00:50:27,546 --> 00:50:28,547
Jiwon.

987
00:50:29,131 --> 00:50:32,092
[panting] What happened?
Are you badly hurt?

988
00:50:32,885 --> 00:50:34,136
No. [sighs]

989
00:50:34,219 --> 00:50:36,930
I was trying to get back into running
and pulled something.

990
00:50:38,474 --> 00:50:40,434
I think it might be broken.

991
00:50:41,435 --> 00:50:42,561
[sighs heavily]

992
00:50:43,687 --> 00:50:45,356
Let's go to the hospital. Hop on.

993
00:50:48,192 --> 00:50:51,403
[chuckles] I'm joking. Honestly.

994
00:50:51,487 --> 00:50:52,780
Sit here.

995
00:50:54,782 --> 00:50:56,659
Are you sure you're okay?

996
00:50:57,326 --> 00:50:58,327
[Dr. Yoon] Mmm.

997
00:50:59,161 --> 00:51:00,245
[♪ gentle, tender music playing]

998
00:51:00,329 --> 00:51:01,914
[both chuckle]

999
00:51:02,831 --> 00:51:04,792
[clears throat] Right now...

1000
00:51:07,252 --> 00:51:10,673
[sighs] ...I just need some comforting.

1001
00:51:20,432 --> 00:51:21,642
[Dr. Yoon chuckles]

1002
00:51:22,976 --> 00:51:24,186
[♪ music fades]
STYLE
::cue()

1003
00:51:26,772 --> 00:51:27,815
[Kyungjin] This looks gorgeous.

1004
00:51:27,898 --> 00:51:29,650
[♪ soft ambient music
playing in background]

1005
00:51:29,733 --> 00:51:31,360
Hey, what are you doing?

1006
00:51:31,443 --> 00:51:33,737
Hey, leave this to me.

1007
00:51:33,821 --> 00:51:37,825
I didn't do anything for you on White Day.
You don't have to lift a finger today.

1008
00:51:40,911 --> 00:51:42,705
Here, open up.

1009
00:51:42,788 --> 00:51:44,415
Leave it. I'll eat it myself.

1010
00:51:44,498 --> 00:51:46,750
-I'm going to eat it.
-[scoffs]

1011
00:51:47,584 --> 00:51:48,585
Whoa!

1012
00:51:48,877 --> 00:51:49,878
It's delicious!

1013
00:51:52,881 --> 00:51:53,882
Mmm!

1014
00:51:58,887 --> 00:52:00,681
It's good, right? Wow!

1015
00:52:00,764 --> 00:52:03,142
Isoo's recommendations never disappoint.

1016
00:52:05,060 --> 00:52:07,354
Babe, you know
we caught Park Jaeha, right?

1017
00:52:07,438 --> 00:52:08,981
Do you know how we did it?

1018
00:52:09,064 --> 00:52:11,233
Sometimes I really think Isoo is a genius.

1019
00:52:11,316 --> 00:52:12,818
-[fork clatters on table]
-No, he is a genius.

1020
00:52:14,945 --> 00:52:16,363
We should break up.

1021
00:52:16,447 --> 00:52:17,448
What?

1022
00:52:18,365 --> 00:52:19,408
What did you just say?

1023
00:52:19,491 --> 00:52:20,993
I want to break up.

1024
00:52:21,076 --> 00:52:22,786
[♪ quirky, dramatic music playing]

1025
00:52:23,871 --> 00:52:25,956
You're breaking up with me over tonkatsu?

1026
00:52:26,039 --> 00:52:27,875
Don't you know why I want to break up?

1027
00:52:28,542 --> 00:52:30,127
I'm asking because I don't.

1028
00:52:30,210 --> 00:52:33,297
[scoffs] Forget it. What more
can I possibly say to you?

1029
00:52:33,380 --> 00:52:34,923
I'm leaving.

1030
00:52:48,103 --> 00:52:50,773
Excuse me. Can you
box up this tonkatsu for me?

1031
00:52:50,856 --> 00:52:53,358
Wow. You're getting it to go right now?

1032
00:52:53,442 --> 00:52:56,361
Hey, the tonkatsu did nothing wrong.

1033
00:52:59,323 --> 00:53:00,657
But still...

1034
00:53:00,741 --> 00:53:02,034
Thank you.

1035
00:53:02,618 --> 00:53:03,994
Uh...

1036
00:53:04,077 --> 00:53:07,039
Have a good life, with your beloved Isoo.

1037
00:53:09,041 --> 00:53:10,042
Bye.

1038
00:53:12,503 --> 00:53:13,754
Wow!

1039
00:53:14,713 --> 00:53:15,756
[scoffs]

1040
00:53:16,256 --> 00:53:17,466
[chuckling]

1041
00:53:20,093 --> 00:53:21,762
-It's still delicious.
-[♪ music fades]

1042
00:53:24,264 --> 00:53:26,892
[sighs wearily] Story of my life.

1043
00:53:26,975 --> 00:53:28,811
Stabbed in the back by guys.

1044
00:53:28,894 --> 00:53:30,145
Time to go home!

1045
00:53:31,522 --> 00:53:33,482
Want to get a drink with me?

1046
00:53:39,988 --> 00:53:40,989
-[Isoo] Cheers.
-[clink]

1047
00:53:41,073 --> 00:53:42,366
[♪ soft jazz music playing in background]

1048
00:53:42,449 --> 00:53:43,492
[slurps]

1049
00:53:43,951 --> 00:53:44,993
[exhales contentedly]

1050
00:53:45,077 --> 00:53:47,496
How's the aroma, huh? Amazing, isn't it?

1051
00:53:48,247 --> 00:53:49,248
[sniffs]

1052
00:53:49,331 --> 00:53:50,541
Yeah, it's amazing.

1053
00:53:50,624 --> 00:53:55,462
[sighs smugly] I spent eight whole months
trying everything to nail this flavor.

1054
00:53:55,546 --> 00:53:57,047
[exhales incredulously]

1055
00:53:57,130 --> 00:53:59,216
I drink soju and beer,
so I can't really tell.

1056
00:53:59,800 --> 00:54:01,593
Oh, you've got no taste.

1057
00:54:01,677 --> 00:54:04,471
Want to try something new?
You can try whiskey starting today.

1058
00:54:04,555 --> 00:54:07,057
No, I'm good. [chuckles]

1059
00:54:07,641 --> 00:54:08,809
[Hyera inhales sharply]

1060
00:54:09,518 --> 00:54:11,478
You even know how to make whiskey.

1061
00:54:11,562 --> 00:54:13,856
You're full of surprises, Jin Isoo.

1062
00:54:13,939 --> 00:54:15,566
What's the matter with you?

1063
00:54:15,649 --> 00:54:19,152
Did another soul fall for my charms? Huh?

1064
00:54:19,236 --> 00:54:20,779
[scoffs, chuckles]

1065
00:54:21,572 --> 00:54:22,573
That said,

1066
00:54:23,907 --> 00:54:26,994
as a cop, you're undeniably
walking a fine line.

1067
00:54:27,077 --> 00:54:28,871
You'll fall if you're not careful.

1068
00:54:28,954 --> 00:54:30,038
Don't worry.

1069
00:54:30,122 --> 00:54:32,666
I was born in the Year of the Monkey.
I'm good at keeping balance.

1070
00:54:32,749 --> 00:54:33,750
[chuckles]

1071
00:54:34,751 --> 00:54:36,712
You just need to use me.

1072
00:54:36,795 --> 00:54:38,589
I'll do anything you need.

1073
00:54:38,672 --> 00:54:40,716
As the cheat code to solving cases.

1074
00:54:40,799 --> 00:54:42,426
Right, cheat code.

1075
00:54:43,635 --> 00:54:44,720
[clink]

1076
00:54:46,263 --> 00:54:47,389
[Isoo exhales softly]

1077
00:54:48,140 --> 00:54:51,310
Will you return to Hansu Group one day?

1078
00:54:51,893 --> 00:54:53,687
Mmm... The truth is...

1079
00:54:53,770 --> 00:54:54,896
[inhales deeply]

1080
00:54:55,606 --> 00:54:57,774
...I dumped it all on Mr. Choi
and ran away.

1081
00:54:58,900 --> 00:55:02,279
He's like an uncle and a father to me,

1082
00:55:03,864 --> 00:55:06,366
but now I'm worried
I put too much on his shoulders.

1083
00:55:06,450 --> 00:55:07,576
[Isoo] Hmm.

1084
00:55:10,329 --> 00:55:11,413
By the way,

1085
00:55:12,497 --> 00:55:15,334
why did you return to Gangha?

1086
00:55:15,417 --> 00:55:17,711
It's odd. You were
doing great at Counterterrorism.

1087
00:55:19,671 --> 00:55:21,381
I have someone I need to catch.

1088
00:55:22,841 --> 00:55:23,884
Who?

1089
00:55:25,385 --> 00:55:27,179
Tell me, we can catch them together.
STYLE
::cue()

1090
00:55:30,599 --> 00:55:31,892
Yu Seongwon.

1091
00:55:31,975 --> 00:55:33,852
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

1092
00:55:33,935 --> 00:55:34,936
Yu Seongwon?

1093
00:55:38,231 --> 00:55:40,359
The Yu Seongwon I know?

1094
00:55:40,442 --> 00:55:41,443
Yes.

1095
00:55:43,570 --> 00:55:45,322
What did he do?

1096
00:55:48,742 --> 00:55:49,785
Serial killings.

1097
00:56:01,254 --> 00:56:02,255
Where is Seongwon?

1098
00:56:02,339 --> 00:56:04,049
At his studio.

1099
00:56:05,759 --> 00:56:06,760
Let's go.

1100
00:56:13,850 --> 00:56:15,435
[♪ suspenseful music continues]

1101
00:56:40,085 --> 00:56:41,253
Chairwoman.

1102
00:56:44,005 --> 00:56:45,757
What brings you all the way here?

1103
00:56:45,841 --> 00:56:47,509
When are you leaving?

1104
00:56:47,592 --> 00:56:48,927
Uh...

1105
00:56:49,010 --> 00:56:51,513
I'm not sure.
I have another exhibition coming up.

1106
00:56:51,596 --> 00:56:52,848
Cancel it and leave.

1107
00:56:53,640 --> 00:56:55,183
That's going to be a problem.

1108
00:56:56,101 --> 00:56:57,894
You see, I can't return to the UK.

1109
00:57:00,981 --> 00:57:02,065
Wow!

1110
00:57:02,941 --> 00:57:04,693
That's a great expression.

1111
00:57:04,776 --> 00:57:06,153
[♪ music increases in tempo]

1112
00:57:06,820 --> 00:57:08,530
Makes me want to sculpt it.

1113
00:57:09,656 --> 00:57:10,699
Wherever it is...

1114
00:57:17,581 --> 00:57:19,791
just pack up and leave quickly.

1115
00:57:22,794 --> 00:57:23,795
Why?

1116
00:57:24,921 --> 00:57:28,008
Do you find it unbearable
that I'm so much like you, Mom?

1117
00:57:28,091 --> 00:57:29,134
[♪ music resumes tempo]

1118
00:57:29,217 --> 00:57:30,343
You know it's true.

1119
00:57:30,427 --> 00:57:32,179
You killed Dad.

1120
00:57:32,262 --> 00:57:33,263
And I...

1121
00:57:33,346 --> 00:57:35,098
uh, wonder...

1122
00:57:35,974 --> 00:57:37,642
[sings] who I killed.

1123
00:57:42,439 --> 00:57:43,607
[chuckles]

1124
00:57:43,690 --> 00:57:46,359
You want to lock me up
in a psych ward again, don't you?

1125
00:57:46,443 --> 00:57:48,779
Because I'm your Achilles' heel.

1126
00:57:49,946 --> 00:57:50,947
But...

1127
00:57:51,948 --> 00:57:53,909
that's not going to happen.

1128
00:57:54,701 --> 00:57:57,621
Your son is famous now.

1129
00:57:57,704 --> 00:57:59,331
[♪ music increases in tempo]

1130
00:58:17,516 --> 00:58:18,600
Leaving so soon?

1131
00:58:19,726 --> 00:58:21,937
Not even a hug
after being apart for four years?

1132
00:58:22,020 --> 00:58:23,855
Are you scared of me?

1133
00:58:25,065 --> 00:58:26,650
-And you call yourself a mother?
-[♪ music swells]

1134
00:58:28,235 --> 00:58:29,820
[♪ music resumes tempo]

1135
00:58:46,253 --> 00:58:47,254
Keep an eye on him

1136
00:58:48,463 --> 00:58:50,298
so he doesn't cause any trouble.

1137
00:58:50,382 --> 00:58:51,466
Yes, ma'am.

1138
00:58:51,550 --> 00:58:53,468
Call me if anything happens.

1139
00:58:53,552 --> 00:58:54,678
Yes, ma'am.

1140
00:58:54,761 --> 00:58:55,971
[♪ tense, pulsating music playing]

1141
00:58:56,054 --> 00:58:57,389
Mr. Hwang.

1142
00:59:06,982 --> 00:59:08,191
I'm counting on you.

1143
00:59:09,442 --> 00:59:10,735
Yes, understood, ma'am.

1144
00:59:22,247 --> 00:59:23,248
[car engine starts]

1145
00:59:27,127 --> 00:59:28,378
[♪ music fades]
STYLE
::cue()

1146
00:59:30,839 --> 00:59:33,049
[♪ gentle piano music
playing in background]

1147
00:59:48,356 --> 00:59:49,399
She's beautiful.

1148
00:59:50,066 --> 00:59:51,234
[chuckles softly]

1149
00:59:51,318 --> 00:59:52,360
[bartender] Who is she?

1150
00:59:53,486 --> 00:59:55,071
Someone who's obsessed with me.

1151
00:59:55,155 --> 00:59:56,156
[chuckles softly]

1152
00:59:56,740 --> 00:59:57,741
Is she a stalker?

1153
00:59:58,575 --> 01:00:00,201
You could say that.

1154
01:00:00,285 --> 01:00:03,371
I'm wondering if I should make her
the model for my next sculpture.

1155
01:00:05,165 --> 01:00:07,250
You're the sculptor, Yu Seongwon, right?

1156
01:00:09,252 --> 01:00:10,629
I went to your exhibition.

1157
01:00:14,966 --> 01:00:16,176
How was it?

1158
01:00:18,386 --> 01:00:19,387
Uh...

1159
01:00:20,889 --> 01:00:23,558
When I was looking at your pieces,

1160
01:00:23,642 --> 01:00:25,518
I almost felt like I couldn't breathe.

1161
01:00:26,519 --> 01:00:27,520
[chuckles softly]

1162
01:00:27,604 --> 01:00:30,607
I felt overwhelmed, I guess.

1163
01:00:31,232 --> 01:00:33,026
[chuckles] You flatter me.

1164
01:00:34,152 --> 01:00:37,530
It felt like there was
some hidden meaning behind it.

1165
01:00:39,658 --> 01:00:41,576
It's all out in the open,

1166
01:00:42,243 --> 01:00:44,204
but not quite revealing the truth.

1167
01:00:45,997 --> 01:00:47,123
You're very perceptive.

1168
01:00:48,500 --> 01:00:50,335
I used to study art.

1169
01:00:51,503 --> 01:00:53,213
I'm taking a break to work.

1170
01:00:53,922 --> 01:00:55,340
Why did you take a break?

1171
01:00:58,093 --> 01:01:00,470
Let's just say, no comment.

1172
01:01:03,014 --> 01:01:06,184
[Hyera] Four years ago,
two of Yu Seongwon's models disappeared.

1173
01:01:06,893 --> 01:01:08,603
And one of his underclassmen.

1174
01:01:09,396 --> 01:01:11,564
They were all closed
as missing persons cases,

1175
01:01:11,648 --> 01:01:14,484
but I think Yu Seongwon killed them.

1176
01:01:14,567 --> 01:01:16,111
[♪ ominous music playing]

1177
01:01:18,613 --> 01:01:19,906
What do you think?

1178
01:01:21,616 --> 01:01:23,284
Is the Yu Seongwon you know

1179
01:01:24,202 --> 01:01:25,578
capable of killing people?

1180
01:01:28,915 --> 01:01:31,292
No, the Seongwon I know

1181
01:01:32,919 --> 01:01:34,963
is timid and soft-hearted.

1182
01:01:36,506 --> 01:01:38,049
Do you have any evidence?

1183
01:01:39,175 --> 01:01:40,802
No, just my gut feeling.

1184
01:01:40,885 --> 01:01:42,637
His alibi checked out.

1185
01:01:42,721 --> 01:01:44,472
[♪ melancholy piano music playing]

1186
01:01:44,556 --> 01:01:46,016
Then it might not be him.

1187
01:01:47,434 --> 01:01:49,894
I was contacted by the UK police recently.

1188
01:01:51,771 --> 01:01:55,066
Two of Yu Seongwon's models are missing.

1189
01:02:05,076 --> 01:02:08,163
I have to submit a piece
for a contemporary art exhibition,

1190
01:02:08,246 --> 01:02:09,914
but I can't seem to find a model.

1191
01:02:09,998 --> 01:02:12,709
Shall I introduce you to someone?

1192
01:02:12,792 --> 01:02:14,919
[♪ tense, foreboding music playing]

1193
01:02:15,003 --> 01:02:16,379
SONG AREUM

1194
01:02:19,883 --> 01:02:21,760
How about you, Areum?
STYLE
::cue()

1195
01:02:31,936 --> 01:02:33,104
Would you

1196
01:02:34,272 --> 01:02:35,648
be my model?

1197
01:02:35,732 --> 01:02:37,150
[♪ music swells]

1198
01:02:49,037 --> 01:02:50,038
FLEX X COP 2
EPISODE 8

1199
01:02:50,121 --> 01:02:51,623
THE TRUTH ABOUT YU SEONGWON COMES TO LIGHT

1200
01:02:51,706 --> 01:02:53,708
[♪ upbeat pop music playing]

1201
01:03:09,224 --> 01:03:12,644
Special Cast. Son Woohyeon

1202
01:03:12,727 --> 01:03:16,147
Special Cast. Jung Chaeyeon

1203
01:03:16,231 --> 01:03:19,651
Special Cast. Heo Sungtae

1204
01:03:30,745 --> 01:03:32,288
-[all scream]
-[Hyera] Who is the deceased student?

1205
01:03:32,372 --> 01:03:35,333
Murder? No student
at our school would do that.

1206
01:03:35,416 --> 01:03:37,335
Was Seyeon alone yesterday?

1207
01:03:37,418 --> 01:03:39,754
[student 1] The principal
supervised her personally.

1208
01:03:39,838 --> 01:03:42,423
-Moon Seyeon's death was a curse.
-A curse?

1209
01:03:42,507 --> 01:03:44,050
Wait, I'll buy you cream puffs!

1210
01:03:44,134 --> 01:03:45,510
We have to focus on the curse.

1211
01:03:45,593 --> 01:03:46,761
[student 2] It's from the Witch Shop.

1212
01:03:46,845 --> 01:03:48,721
-Who do you want to curse?
-The police.

1213
01:03:48,805 --> 01:03:49,848
Why would the police...

1214
01:03:49,931 --> 01:03:52,392
[Hyera] Someone hated Moon Seyeon.

1215
01:03:52,475 --> 01:03:54,185
-[student 3] A senior died last year.
-A ghost?

1216
01:03:54,269 --> 01:03:55,353
Stay back!

1217
01:03:55,436 --> 01:03:56,813
-[Kyungjin] The CCTVs?
-[man] They were down.

1218
01:03:56,896 --> 01:03:58,398
It makes no sense.

1219
01:03:59,065 --> 01:04:00,692
They're still at the school.

1220
01:04:00,775 --> 01:04:01,776
[both gasp]

1221
01:04:01,860 --> 01:04:04,445
Be careful. Someone's after you.

1222
01:04:04,529 --> 01:04:05,530
That's a secret.

1223
01:04:05,613 --> 01:04:08,116
[woman] I have a bad feeling about this.

1224
01:04:14,622 --> 01:04:16,916
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

1225
01:04:17,000 --> 01:04:18,751
CONTACT ANALYSIS: YU SEONGWON

1226
01:04:22,005 --> 01:04:24,924
VICTIM 3: KIM HEEJUN
MISSING SINCE 16 SEP 2021

1227
01:04:33,266 --> 01:04:34,642
[cell phone vibrating]

1228
01:04:41,691 --> 01:04:43,735
[in English] Yes, this is Joo Hyera.

1229
01:04:45,111 --> 01:04:47,071
Yes, I requested the file.

1230
01:04:49,741 --> 01:04:50,950
Two people.

1231
01:04:51,034 --> 01:04:52,368
Are they missing?

1232
01:04:55,580 --> 01:04:56,581
Right.

1233
01:04:57,874 --> 01:04:59,667
I understand. Thank you.

1234
01:05:03,838 --> 01:05:04,923
[line disconnects]

1235
01:05:07,258 --> 01:05:08,426
[sighs wearily]

1236
01:05:18,937 --> 01:05:20,939
Translated by Hyesoo Lee

